{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` is 791 LOC (9 under the 800 cap). It flatly mixes three layers: the public append/commit **API**, git-failure **recovery** routines, and low-level git **subprocess primitives**. Recovery logic (transient-add retry, unmerged-index recovery, invalid-object recovery) is the recurring growth driver here. Zero in-progress contention. Flagged by audit ae1b.\n\n## Approach\nSplit into three modules along the existing layer boundary, establishing an explicit one-way dependency direction — API → recovery → git primitives — so new git-error-recovery code lands in the recovery module instead of re-inflating the API file (the recurrence-preventing fix). All moved symbols are private (`_`-prefixed), so only intra-package imports change — no external call sites and no re-exports needed.\n\n1. Extract **git subprocess primitives** → new `src/rebar/_store/event_append_git.py` (~150 LOC): `_run_git` (event_append.py:246), `_git_add` (:263), `_git_commit` (:287), `_git_rm` (:312), `_git_commit_paths` (:324), `_with_transient_add_retry` (:202), `_is_transient_add_error` (:197).\n2. Extract **failure-recovery routines** → new `src/rebar/_store/event_append_recovery.py` (~170 LOC): `_recover_from_unmerged` (:672), `_recover_from_invalid_object` (:740), `_is_invalid_object_error` (:727), `_staged_index_paths` (:732), `_rollback_batch` (:621), `_restore_paths` (:346), `_unstage` (:650), `_silent_unlink` (:642).\n3. `event_append.py` retains the **public API + validation/prep**: `StoreError` (:107), `event_filename` (:115), `_ensure_initialized` (:120), `_validate_event` (:126), `_prepare_event` (:148), `delete_events` (:356), `stage_and_commit` (:397), `batch_stage_and_commit` (:479), `write_and_push` (:575), `batch_write_and_push` (:605), `_maybe_enrich_drain` (:631) → ~471 LOC.\n\nRationale (G6): the layers have distinct change-drivers and a natural acyclic dependency (API calls recovery on failure; recovery calls primitives) — the split makes that direction explicit and testable. The public API surface (`stage_and_commit`, `write_and_push`, `batch_write_and_push`, `delete_events`, imported by `_store/push.py`, `_store/ensures.py`, the reconciler, and `_commands/*`) stays in `event_append.py`, so no external importer changes and the edit-set stays non-overlapping.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` — keep public API + validation; import the two new modules.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append_git.py` — NEW (git subprocess primitives).\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append_recovery.py` — NEW (git-failure recovery).\n\n## Verification (behavior-preserving refactor)\n- `event_append.py` ≤ 500 LOC; module-size + type + lint gates green.\n- Existing oracles pass unchanged: `tests/unit/test_push_callers_best_effort.py`, `tests/unit/test_store_delete_events.py`, and the store/concurrency suites.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` ≤ 500; both new modules ≥ 100 LOC.\n- [ ] No import cycle among the three modules (API → recovery → git only), verified by `python -c \"import rebar._store.event_append\"` succeeding and `import rebar._store.event_append_git` not importing the other two.\n- [ ] All prior public import paths resolve unchanged (`python -c \"from rebar._store.event_append import stage_and_commit, write_and_push, batch_write_and_push, delete_events\"`).\n- [ ] Full default suite and all gates green with no test edits."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786220827109937001,"uuid":"daa7f62c-c3a0-4d15-a3f9-6554d43a359c"}